---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';

// DRAFT privacy notice in plain language, written to match what this site actually does today
// (no cookies, no analytics, no third-party scripts; fonts and images are self-hosted).
// Not legal advice — have it reviewed, and update it when you add a payment provider, form tool, or analytics.
const UPDATED = '12 November 2026';
---

<Layout title="Privacy · Udaan Foundation" description="How Udaan Foundation handles personal information.">
	<main class="px-6 pt-12 pb-24 lg:px-12 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-36">
		<div class="max-w-6xl">
			<p class="font-ui text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] text-stone-500 uppercase" data-reveal>Privacy</p>
			<h1
				class="text-ink mt-3 max-w-3xl font-serif text-5xl leading-[1.02] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance md:text-6xl"
				data-reveal
				style="--delay: 80ms"
			>
				Your information, in plain language.
			</h1>
			<p class="font-ui mt-6 text-[13px] text-stone-500" data-reveal style="--delay: 160ms">Last updated {UPDATED}</p>
		</div>

		<article class="prose-udaan mt-14 max-w-2xl lg:mt-20" data-reveal>
			<p>
				Udaan Foundation is run by students, and we try to collect as little about you as possible. This page explains what
				we collect, why, and what you can do about it.
			</p>

			<h2>Browsing this site</h2>
			<p>
				This website doesn't use cookies, analytics, or advertising trackers, and it doesn't load anything from other
				companies' servers while you browse. Like any website, our hosting provider may keep basic technical logs (such as
				IP addresses) for security and reliability.
			</p>

			<h2>Donations</h2>
			<p>
				Donations are handled by a third-party payment provider. When you give, the provider collects your payment details
				under its own privacy policy, and shares with us the information we need to thank you and keep records, such as your
				name, email address, and the amount you gave. We never see or store your full card details.
			</p>

			<h2>Applications from organizations</h2>
			<p>
				If you apply for funding, you'll fill in a form hosted by a third-party form provider. We use what you send, such as
				contact details, information about your organization, and photos, only to review your application and, if we
				partner, to tell your story with your permission.
			</p>

			<h2>When you email us</h2>
			<p>We keep your messages so we can reply and follow up. We don't add you to any mailing list unless you ask.</p>

			<h2>Photos of children</h2>
			<p>
				Photos on this site are shared with us by our partner organizations. We only publish photos of children when our
				partners confirm that a parent or guardian has agreed. If you'd like a photo removed, contact us and we'll take it down.
			</p>

			<h2>What we never do</h2>
			<p>We don't sell or rent personal information, and we don't share it with anyone except the services described above.</p>

			<h2>Your choices</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask us what information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, at any time.
				{
					CONTACT_EMAIL ? (
						<>
							Email{' '}
							<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
							{' '}and we'll respond as soon as we can.
						</>
					) : (
						<>Get in touch using the contact details on this site and we'll respond as soon as we can.</>
					)
				}
			</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>If we change how we handle information, we'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
